# Rust workspace artifacts (defense-in-depth; component .gitignores cover this too)
**/target/
**/*.rs.bk

# Working backups made during edits (*.rs.bak, *.rs.bak-<tag>) — local only.
**/*.rs.bak*

# Throwaway probe/replay harnesses (tmp_* prefix) — local dev tooling.
/kuluu-render/tests/tmp_*.rs


# Root release exe — build artifact, ~120MB (over GitHub's 100MB blob limit).
# Regenerate: cargo build -p kuluu --release && logs/sync_exe.ps1
/kuluu.exe

# Node / abandoned scaffolds
**/node_modules/

# Python bytecode (scripts/*.py)
**/__pycache__/
*.pyc

# OS / editor
.DS_Store
*.swp
*.swo
.idea/

# Claude Code per-user settings + plugin runtime state
.claude/settings.local.json
.claude/.*/

# OpenCode / sibling-agent harness session state — ephemeral, per-user.
.omo/
.omc/

# Environment / credentials
.env
.env.local
*.env

# Logs
*.log
log/
/logs/
/play_cowland.bat

# jacq build output — regenerate via `jacq build` in ffxi-agent/.
ffxi-agent/dist/

# FFXI client DATs — SE-copyrighted, NEVER commit. Local copy of the user's
# HorizonXI install lives here (see ffxi-dat/README or the async-watching-waffle
# plan for layout). See README "Getting the game files"; FFXI_DAT_PATH points at
# vendor/game-files/SquareEnix/FINAL FANTASY XI/.
vendor/game-files/

# xi-tinkerer — vendored as AGPL-3 reference only (read-only, never linked).
# See vendor/xi-tinkerer/CLAIM.md and memory note `xi_tinkerer_agpl_reference`.
vendor/xi-tinkerer/

# RZN MapViewer (galkareeve/ffxi backup) — STRICT cite-only. NO LICENSE in repo,
# and mapViewer/mapViewer/model_ff11.cpp is verbatim Noesis plugin source
# (Rich Whitehouse, "all rights to be taken to the grave"). Treat as
# all-rights-reserved: do NOT copy, derive, paste, or link from any crate.
# See vendor/RZN-mapviewer/CLAIM.md and memory note `rzn_mapviewer_cite_only`.
vendor/RZN-mapviewer/

# XIM browser FFXI client (GPL-3) — read-only feature reference, NEVER commit.
# Fetch a local copy with `research/fetch-xim.sh`. See research/README.md.
research/xim/
# Phoenix server (GPL-3) — private upstream, so not a submodule. Clone it here
# yourself for the wire-protocol divergence signal. See research/AGENTS.md.
research/Phoenix/
# stray top-level copy (older fetch location)
/xim/
.functional-emotions
.claude/worktrees/

# WASM build outputs — each bundle is ~150MB and exceeds GitHub's 100MB
# blob limit. Regenerate locally via the wasm toolchain.
ffxi-viewer-wasm/dist/
profile.json.gz

# Container-built Linux binaries (docker/build-linux.sh)
/dist/

# Beads / Dolt files (added by bd init)
.dolt/
*.db
.beads-credential-key
.beads/proxieddb/

# skill-creator eval scratch (transient benchmark runs)
.agents/skills/*-workspace/

# Verification evidence marker (stop.d/25-verify.sh gate) — per-machine,
# ephemeral by design: stale the moment gated source is edited after it.
.verify/

# Retail-client captures (retail-observe skill) — SE-copyrighted, reference
# only, NEVER commit. Same rationale as vendor/game-files/ above.
/artifacts/retail/
artifacts/

# Chrome/Perfetto traces from --features trace runs — runtime artifacts
/trace-*.json

# CowEngine import (2026-08-22) — the old C++ client engine moved over wholesale
# from C:\CowEngine. Not yet part of this workspace; keep out until we decide what
# to absorb into the Rust crates. data/roms inside is ~11GB SE-copyrighted retail
# DATs (same rationale as vendor/game-files/ above).
/cow_ashita_module_examples/
/docs/
/extracted_dats/
/cow_tools/
/Archived_cowengine/

*.bak-speedup
speedup.ps1
